  "solution": "**Given:**\n\nWe need to find the value of **tan(255°)**.\n\n**Formula used:**\n\ntan(255°) can be written as tan(180° + 75°), using the identity:\n\ntan(180° + ×) = tan(×)\n\n**Calculation:**\n\ntan(255°) = tan(180° + 75°)\n\n⇒ tan(255°) = tan(75°)\n\n**Now,**\n\ntan(A + B) = (tanA + tanB) / (1 - tanA × tanB)\n\nLet A = 45° and B = 30°, so:\n\ntan(75°) = tan(45° + 30°) = (tan(45°) + tan(30°)) / (1 - tan(45°) × tan(30°))\n\n⇒ tan(75°) = (1 + 1/√3) / (1 - 1 × 1/√3)\n\n⇒ tan(75°) = (1 + 1/√3) / (1 - 1/√3)\n\n⇒ tan(75°) = (√3 + 1) / (√3 - 1)\n\n⇒ tan(75°) = [(√3 + 1) × (√3 + 1)] / [(√3 - 1) × (√3 + 1)]\n\n⇒ tan(75°) = (3 + 2√3 + 1) / (3 - 1)\n\n⇒ tan(75°) = (4 + 2√3) / 2\n\n⇒ tan(75°) = 2 + √3\n\nThe value of tan(255°) is **2 + √3**.",
